  "valuation_insights": "Apple Inc.'s fiscal year 2026 total revenue was $478,834 million, showing a growth of approximately 15.06% from $416,161 million in fiscal 2025 [C:revenue2026] [C:revenue_growth2026]. Operating income reached $158,063 million, resulting in an operating margin of 33.0% [C:operating_income2026] [C:operating_margin2026]. Net income attributable to the company was $132,175 million with GAAP diluted EPS at $8.98 [C:net_income2026] [C:diluted_eps2026]. Return on average equity was notably high at 142.3% [C:return_on_average_equity2026]. The debt to equity ratio, including the current portion of debt, stood at 0.70 [C:debt_to_equity2026]. Free cash flow amounted to $136,056 million [C:free_cash_flow2026].\n\nIn the quarter ended September 26, 2026 (Q4 2026), Apple reported revenue of $114,477 million, marking a 12% year-over-year increase [C:latest_quarter_revenue]. GAAP diluted EPS for this quarter was $2.10 [C:latest_quarter_eps]. Using the closing stock price on October 30, 2026 of $344.63, the fiscal 2026 P/E ratio is approximately 38.38 [C:pe_ratio].\n\nRegarding peers, Microsoft's operating margin for CY2026 was significantly higher at 46.8%, while Alphabet Inc. and Oracle Corp. reported operating margins of 32.0% and 30.6% respectively, all based on consistent total revenue definitions [C:msft_operating_margin] [C:googl_operating_margin] [C:orcl_operating_margin].",
